Description: CONTROLGUI - Minecraft server panel as a native app
 The same web panel (Node.js, no npm dependencies) to manage real Minecraft
 servers, but opened as a NATIVE desktop window via WebKitGTK (like the Windows
 WebView2 wrapper) instead of a browser. A separate entry among applications.
 .
 Includes both launchers: "controlgui-app" (native window, default menu entry)
 and "controlgui" (browser / app mode). Server data is stored under the user's
 home (~/.local/share/controlgui). Needs a Java runtime to run servers and
 libarchive-tools (bsdtar) to read .jar metadata.
